alex: Quick note: opened a compact PR to align streaming + pagination snippets across py/ts/go. Target is copy-pasteable examples showing AbortController/ctx cancel, small retry/backoff, and a tiny pagination-with-stream example. PR: https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/5042

jia: Nice. I'll validate that the pagination snippet distinguishes between a streaming cursor (partial stream token) vs the normal page cursor. People mix those up. Also check the python async iterator style.

sam: For Go please show signal.NotifyContext usage and a compact retry wrapper. Many folks pasted previous examples and leaked goroutines on Ctrl-C. Keep the Go sample short so it fits inline.

tmiller: Reminder: runtime rename landed last sprint. New config shape in JS/Py is `retries.max_attempts`. Go client still uses `MaxRetries` until its next client bump. Docs should show the new shape and a one-line compatibility note for Go.

alex: Plan: docs will show canonical new shape in JS/Py, and a compact Go note like `// Go: MaxRetries until client vX`. I'll add a migration blurb.

alex: Draft TS snippet (short):
```
// ts stream minimal
const ac = new AbortController();
setTimeout(() => ac.abort(), 20_000);
try {
  for await (const chunk of client.stream({ model: 'rw/fast-13b', retries: { max_attempts: 3 }, signal: ac.signal })) {
    process.stdout.write(chunk.text);
  }
} catch (e) {
  console.error('stream failed', e);
}
```

jia: Add a one-line note above the snippet: "Partial chunks are emitted in request order; do not assume batching will reorder the stream." Link to examples/test_stream_order.py for the simple test.

sam: Proposed Go compact pattern to paste into docs:
```
// go: stream_retry.go (compact)
ctx, stop := signal.NotifyContext(context.Background(), os.Interrupt)
defer stop()
opts := StreamOptions{Model: "rw/fast-13b", MaxRetries: 3} // Go client pre-vX
for attempt := 0; attempt < 5; attempt++ {
  if err := runStream(ctx, opts); err == nil || ctx.Err() != nil { break }
  time.Sleep(time.Duration(math.Pow(2, float64(attempt))) * 150 * time.Millisecond)
}
```

tmiller: Looks good. In migration.md mention "runtime >=2.1 uses retries.max_attempts for JS/Py; Go client will follow in client vX" and link the runtime PR. I'll add a short note in the release notes.

alex: Good. Also adding a tiny python test snippet to examples:
```
# examples/test_stream_order.py
def test_order(client):
    seqs = [c.seq for c in client.stream({ 'model': 'rw/fast-13b' })]
    assert seqs == sorted(seqs)
```

jia: Perfect. Also reference eng-runtime/backoff.md and mention full-jitter as recommended for production. I'll add a short inline link next to the retry examples.

sam: Pushed a compact commit that swaps the Go example to use NotifyContext and the compact retry loop. Commit id 6b9a2d. Preview should update.

